WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.330
Welcome to the Transhuman Daily, Wednesday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.990
Here are the last 24 hours in transhumanism, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.510
Trial and error! An Alzheimer's pill missed overall,

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.950
but slowed decline by nearly a third in one group.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.740
And in a ten-person trial, MDMA therapy cut veterans' PTSD from severe to mild.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.830
OpenAI's new Astra is its first public mode

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.790
l rated high for helping improve AI itself.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.390
Google's Gemini Tasks, an agent that calls businesses,

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.170
books appointments and shops, is now free.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.570
Microsoft says its new MAI Code 2 nearly

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.340
matches rivals at a fraction of the cost.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:58.010
And grant pitches written with more AI help stuck closer to ideas already funded,

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:58.950
a study found.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.150
On to longevity.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:07.520
A leukaemia vaccine lifted typical survival from 15 months to two years, its maker says.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.800
And a light and sound headset for Alzheimer's missed too,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.170
though milder cases hinted at a benefit.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:15.580
In a dish,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:20.530
Yamanaka's team found turning back a cell's clock doesn't always make it work better.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.810
Closer to home, a Wollongong-led team is building corneas in the lab,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.820
with first tests due next year.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.280
On to wellbeing. In a small trial,

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.420
psilocybin eased the loss of joy in hard-to-treat depression.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.110
And an AI that watches how you walk spotted links to sleep,

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.820
mood and even liver health.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.900
Now, the catch.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:51.270
Interpol and the UN warn brain-reading tests in police interviews aren't proven to work.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.450
And OpenAI's own tests found Astra kept quiet

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.540
about known problems twice as often as before.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.190
On Saturday, China's all-electric,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.860
19-seat airliner flew with a crew for the first time.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:13.830
Boston Dynamics' Atlas humanoid heads into chip factories for testing next year,

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.550
its first beyond carmakers.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.100
Oh,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:20.500
and physicists found a way to put error bars on quantum machines too big to check.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.870
Some trials miss, some win,

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.750
and each one moves us forward. That's trial and error.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.550
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.710
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.350
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.340
That's the Transhuman Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.330
Stay well. Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
